    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Christian Yelich** (70.77) and **Junior Caminero** (68.21) anchoring the lineup, both benefiting significantly from favorable matchups against right-handed pitching. **Christian Yelich** remains a primary target due to his 13% dynamic platoon boost against Singer, while **Junior Caminero**\u2019s presence in the three-hole against Lambert provides the necessary power upside to anchor the middle of the order. While **Pete Crow-Armstrong** faces a difficult task against Skenes (3.33 xERA), his 65.79 score is bolstered by a massive 14% platoon edge and a +5% wind-out factor, making him an essential start despite the SP\u2019s pedigree; his elite speed remains our best weapon to capitalize on the Zebras' scarcity-focused roster strategy.\n\nConversely, we are treading carefully with **Yordan Alvarez** (46.83). Despite his elite 0.443 xwOBA, the combination of a lefty-on-lefty matchup against Seymour and a projected 19% hit to his projection due to the SP's skill profile drags his score to the bottom of our active starters. The toughest omission on our bench is **Carson Benge** (48.42); he finished just shy of the active roster threshold. While **Carson Benge** received a +7% platoon boost, the optimizer favored the higher efficiency floors offered by **Josh Smith** and **Caleb Durbin**, whose respective plate appearances provide more consistent access to stolen base opportunities\u2014our highest priority category. \n\nRisk remains elevated across the board as several slots, including **Gary Sanchez**, **Yordan Alvarez**, and **Lars Nootbaar**, currently operate under \"Lineup Pending\" status. While we have projected them based on historical order, any shift downward in the batting order for **Lars Nootbaar** or **Gary Sanchez** will further suppress their already marginal scores. Managers should monitor these late-breaking lineups closely, as any unexpected benching for **Hector Rodriguez** or the other pending positions will necessitate an immediate pivot to our bench depth, led by **Chase Meidroth** or **Jacob Gonzalez**, to maintain our daily game cap efficiency.",
